WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Every bean began with a pollen
grain landing on a flower's stigma.

2
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:08.460
A tube grew down from it,
digesting a path with enzymes,

3
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.210
to reach the egg cell inside an ovule.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.960
The result was an embryo,
sealed inside a seed coat,

5
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.210
then dried out and dormant.

6
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.730
A dry bean can sit in a jar for years,
then sprout within days of getting wet.

7
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.190
What powers that first growth?

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.540
In this mission, you'll follow a
pollen grain all the way to an embryo.

9
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.670
Then you'll see which parts
of a flower become the seed,

10
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.380
and which become the fruit.

11
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: find out what powers a dry
bean's first growth once it gets wet.
